<div class="head"><span class="eyebrow rv">Why we build products</span><h2 class="split">Why a services company builds products.</h2></div>
<div class="g3">
<div class="card rv"><span class="tag">On call</span><h3>We carry our own pager.</h3><p>When our product breaks, we fix it. That's the standard we bring to systems we run for clients.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d:100ms"><span class="tag">Real users</span><h3>We design for real users.</h3><p>Hotel supervisors on a busy floor and people using screen readers don't forgive vague interfaces.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d:200ms"><span class="tag">Honesty</span><h3>We say what's proven.</h3><p>Our product pages use illustrative data until real results exist. Our client pages follow the same rule.</p></div>
</div></div></div>
